@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-5 border-bottom border-subtle pb-4">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3">About Me</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose fs-5 lh-lg text-muted">
        <p>
            Hi, I'm <strong class="text-main">Okewale Akintunde Oluleke</strong>—a Software Engineer, Software Architect, and Engineering Leader with over two decades of experience building enterprise software and solving complex business problems.
        </p>

        <p>
            Throughout my career, I've designed and delivered systems across fintech, banking, government, healthcare, HR, and enterprise platforms. My passion lies at the intersection of software architecture, cloud-native engineering, AI, and product development.
        </p>

        <p>
            This blog is where I document what I learn, what I build, and what I wish someone had taught me earlier.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 mb-2 fw-medium text-main">You'll find practical articles on:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4">
            <li>Software Architecture and System Design</li>
            <li>.NET, C#, ASP.NET Core, and Azure</li>
            <li>AI Engineering and AI-Native Applications</li>
            <li>Cloud Computing and DevOps</li>
            <li>APIs and Distributed Systems</li>
            <li>Software Engineering Best Practices</li>
            <li>Engineering Leadership</li>
            <li>Product Development and SaaS</li>
            <li>Fintech and Digital Banking</li>
            <li>Career Growth for Software Engineers</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            I believe great software isn't just about writing code—it's about understanding problems deeply, making thoughtful design decisions, and building systems that remain reliable as they evolve.
        </p>

        <p>
            Many of the articles here are based on real-world experience: lessons learned from building production systems, leading engineering teams, reviewing architectures, and navigating the challenges of enterprise software development.
        </p>

        <p>
            I also enjoy exploring emerging technologies, especially how artificial intelligence is transforming software engineering. As AI reshapes the industry, I believe engineers must evolve from simply writing code to designing intelligent, scalable, and resilient systems.
        </p>

        <p>
            Whether you're a student, a junior developer, a seasoned architect, or an engineering leader, my goal is to provide practical insights you can apply immediately—not just theory.
        </p>

        <p>
            When I'm not designing software or writing code, you'll usually find me researching new technologies, reading technical books, experimenting with new ideas, or working on products that solve meaningful problems.
        </p>

        <p>
            If something I write helps you solve a problem, teaches you something new, or inspires your next project, then this blog has achieved its purpose.
        </p>

        <p class="fw-bold mt-5 text-main">
            Welcome, and thanks for stopping by.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
